---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import deliveryImage from "../assets/dumpster-delivery.jpg";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { business } from "../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Dumpster Rentals Haines City"
  description="Learn how Dumpster Rentals Haines City approaches project planning, customer communication, safety, and local roll-off container service."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About our service</p>
      <h1>Clear guidance for a cleaner project</h1>
      <p>
        Dumpster Rentals Haines City connects local cleanup needs with practical roll-off container planning. We focus on the details that help delivery, loading, and pickup go more smoothly.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/contact/">Request a Free Estimate</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container media-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why we are here</p>
        <h2>Waste removal should support the work, not slow it down</h2>
        <p>
          Cleanup is rarely the main reason someone starts a project. Homeowners want to reclaim a room, prepare for a move, or improve a property. Contractors need to complete the next phase. Business teams need to reset a space while protecting daily operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Debris still needs a plan. Without one, material can take over driveways, work areas, parking spaces, and access routes. Our role is to help customers in Haines City think through temporary dumpster service before waste becomes an obstacle.
        </p>
        <p>
          We start with questions: What are you removing? How large is the project area? What kind of surface and access does the site offer? When do you expect to load the container? Are any materials dense, bulky, restricted, or uncertain?
        </p>
        <p>
          Those answers create a better foundation for a container recommendation and free estimate. They also give you a chance to understand material rules, fill limits, placement considerations, and pickup access before delivery day.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="media-frame">
        <Image
          src={deliveryImage}
          alt="Roll-off dumpster service truck delivering a container in Haines City"
          width={896}
          height={504}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          quality={55}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cream">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our core values</p>
      <h2>Principles that guide every customer conversation</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Integrity</h3>
          <p>We want customers to understand the information behind a rental plan. Clear questions and direct expectations help people make informed decisions.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Quality</h3>
          <p>Quality service comes from attention to the whole process: project details, placement, access, material guidance, scheduling, and communication.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Excellence</h3>
          <p>We aim to make each step useful and easy to follow. That means listening closely, explaining practical details, and treating every request with care.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Safety</h3>
          <p>We encourage clear delivery routes, suitable placement areas, contained loads, respected fill lines, and honest disclosure of questionable material.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid--2">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you can expect</p>
        <h2>A conversation built around your project</h2>
        <p>
          You do not need to arrive with perfect measurements or know the name of a container size. Start with what you know. Describe the rooms, work area, debris, site, and timing. If the scope is still changing, say so.
        </p>
        <p>
          We will help organize those details into a practical discussion. For a residential cleanout, that may mean bulky household items and driveway placement. For construction, weight and job-site access may matter more. For a commercial property, operating hours and shared traffic can shape the plan.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also encourage customers to ask questions. Confirm accepted material before loading. Discuss a surface that concerns you. Mention wires, branches, gates, slopes, or narrow approaches. Good information protects the schedule.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local focus</p>
        <h2>Serving one community with relevant information</h2>
        <p>
          This website focuses on dumpster rental in Haines City, Florida. We do not publish dozens of nearly identical city pages or claim a storefront address that does not exist. Our public contact details stay consistent across the site so customers know how to reach us.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also avoid invented reviews, inflated history, and unsupported promises. Trust grows when the service information answers real questions and the estimate reflects the project a customer actually describes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Browse our <a href="/">dumpster rental guide</a> or compare residential, construction, and commercial service pages. When you are ready, call <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phoneDisplay}</a> or send your details online.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Tell us what your cleanup needs"
    text="Share your project, material, placement, and timing. We will help you take the next step with a free estimate."
  />
</BaseLayout>
